# API standards

Public HTTP API under **`/api/**`**. Resource-oriented paths, nouns not verbs; use HTTP methods for actions. Version in path or header only when product requires it—stay consistent across endpoints.

## Request and response

- **Explicit DTOs** for every request body and response body (records or immutable types). Controllers return DTOs or `ResponseEntity<Dto>`—never **`@Entity`** or lazy-loaded graphs.
- **Jakarta Bean Validation** on inputs (`@Valid`, constraints on DTOs and `@RequestParam`/`@PathVariable` where applicable). Validation failures → **400** with field-level detail in ProblemDetail extensions (e.g. `errors[]` with `field`, `message`).
- Keep OpenAPI (springdoc) in sync with DTOs and status codes; breaking changes need explicit review.

## HTTP status codes

| Situation | Status |
|-----------|--------|
| Success with body | **200** (GET/PUT/PATCH), **201** + `Location` when creating |
| Success, no body | **204** |
| Validation / bad input | **400** |
| Missing or invalid auth | **401** |
| Authenticated, not allowed | **403** |
| Missing resource | **404** |
| State conflict (e.g. illegal transition) | **409** |
| Unexpected server fault | **500** (generic detail only) |

Use **409** for business rule conflicts, not **400**, when input is syntactically valid but operation is rejected.

## Errors (RFC 9457)

- All error responses use **`ProblemDetail`** (`application/problem+json`). Stable **`type`** URI or slug per error class; human-readable **`title`** and **`detail`** safe for UI display.
- Map domain exceptions in **`@ControllerAdvice`**—never leak stack traces, SQL, or class names. Log full cause server-side only.
- Frontend needs actionable messages: clear `detail`, optional machine-readable `code` extension; same shape for every endpoint.

## Boundaries

- Services throw domain exceptions; controllers do not catch-and-swallow into generic 200.
- Do not serialize internal types (entities, `Optional` leaks, Hibernate proxies). Map in service or dedicated mapper layer before response.
